<title>HONG KONG: China Travel in HK$2.6 bln power project.</title>
<headline>China Travel in HK$2.6 bln power project.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Travel International Investment Hong Kong Ltd said on Thursday its 30 percent owned Chadwick Developments Ltd had agreed to buy a 51 percent stake in Weihe Power Station Project in Shaanxi Province for HK$2.58 billion.</p>
<p>Chadwick is 70 percent owned by China Travel International's controlling shareholder China Travel Service (Holding) Hong Kong Ltd.</p>
<p>The company said the stake was bought from a Chinese partner in the power plant, Electric Power Construction Investment and Development Corp of Shaanxi Province.</p>
<p>The project was originally 70 percent held by Electric Power Construction and 30 percent by China North-West Electric Power Group Co.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
